Z||000000||AgaricX||10-31-2001||01:05 AM||||No, not the widest people you've seen driving Fieros.<P>What are the widest rear tires that you have currently or have had on your Fiero?  I want wider tires for that agressive look, but how wide should I get on 17"s||||reg||1
Z||000001||BlackStang95||10-31-2001||01:07 AM||||i think 275's are the best.  Lotsa traction.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rick 88||10-31-2001||01:24 AM||||I am running a 215/45 front and 245/45 rear 17 in combo on my 88 GT. Wheels are 17x7.5 .40 offset. The tires fill the openings equally front and rear and do not stick out. I have the front lowered about 1.25 inches. A 255/45 will still clear on an 88 but the speedo will be too far off. On pre 88's check the inner strut clearance even with the 245's.<P>Rick 88||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroX||10-31-2001||02:22 AM||||rare87gt put 245/60/15's on the rear of his and they fit perfect, so id imagine any comparable 245, say a 50/16 or 45/17 or 40/18 will be the same.  he doesnt have any clearance issues, they dont stick out, and that is on the stock 15" snowflake style rims.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://luminasupercharged.com/logo1small.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||10-31-2001||02:59 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rick 88:<BR><B>I am running a 215/45 front and 245/45 rear 17 in combo on my 88 GT. Wheels are 17x7.5 .40 offset. The tires fill the openings equally front and rear and do not stick out. I have the front lowered about 1.25 inches. A 255/45 will still clear on an 88 but the speedo will be too far off. On pre 88's check the inner strut clearance even with the 245's.<P>Rick 88</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Got Pics? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||10-31-2001||08:49 AM||||i have 255/50-16's on 7.5" rims on my '87 but you need to switch to coilovers. and 235/50-16 on my '86 gt that i may try on the front of my '87. got some 245/45-16's off ebay that if i ever get (deals getting strange) i will be putting on the same size wheel for the '86. i went with 16's for price and working on a size i like that hopefully all the cars will end up with so i can interchange.<P> <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChopTop||10-31-2001||09:46 AM||||About how much wider can you expect to go if you get coilovers?  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||10-31-2001||10:01 AM||||According to the FAQ on West Coast Fiero's website, you can run 255/40-17's on a 17x9" rim with a 45mm offset on the back.  They do say you have to run a 17" rim, as a 16" rim will hit the strut at this size.||||reg||1
Z||000008||88 Fiero||10-31-2001||11:48 AM||||On a 17X9 wheels in the rear...you can shove 265X35 or 30's it would fit without a problem..||||reg||1
