Z||000011||LT1 Chop Top||10-31-2001||05:10 PM||||I have 255-40-17 Rear (17x9) and 225-45-16 Front (16x7.5) on my 88 GT.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt11_2.jpg"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||DKOV||10-31-2001||07:45 PM||||EDIT - Oops... forgot the pic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> - EDIT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=45044&a=304393&p=52272875&Sequence=0"> <P>225's in front with 235s in the rear on 17 inch Koenig rims wrapped in Yokohama AVS Sport tires.<P>I used to have a set of 285s on the rear of my 86 GT but the rim tended to "swim" in the tire at higher speeds.  Those tires were Goodyear GT II if I remember right.  The fronts were also 225's then.<P>The AVS Sports have a TON more grip even though they are more narrow.  Less rotating mass too   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>DKOV -<p>[This message has been edited by DKOV (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||1
